/target
/dist
/dist-papers
# Output-isolated dirs for the publish-* family so it runs concurrently with
# tauri-run without clobbering dist/ + target/ (Makefile DIST/TARGET_DIR).
# **A GLOB, not an enumeration.** This list used to name each publish output
# directory one at a time, so every NEW one was committable by default — and
# that is exactly how one 2026-08-21 chat fix swept in 18,408 files: a 114 MB
# `dist-all/` publish tree plus an 11 MB frozen SPA shell, neither of which any
# target regenerates under those names. Same shape as the cache-header rule this
# repo already learned: when a policy enumerates the exceptions and defaults the
# rest to the unsafe value, everything added later inherits the unsafe value
# silently. Nothing under a `dist-` prefix is source; if that ever stops being
# true, negate the one path rather than going back to a list.
/dist-*
/dist-publish
/dist-federation
/dist-registry
# The uploadable production web tree (`make site-dist` / SITE_DIST_OUT). Built,
# never committed — and deliberately NOT under dist/, which trunk wipes.
/dist-site
/target-publish
# Transient staging dirs for `make tauri-bundle` — the recipe copies an external
# APPS_DIST / INGEST here so the publish container (which mounts only this repo)
# can see them, then removes them. Never committed.
/.apps-stage
/.ingest-stage
# Durable publisher identity (Makefile PUBLISH_DATA_DIR / ENTITY_DATA_DIR) — a
# private keypair; NEVER commit it. The glob matters: the registry emitter
# resolves a SEPARATE durable identity (`{data-dir}-registry/`, so that a
# name-issuer key is not also a content-publisher key), and `/.entity-publish`
# alone does not match `/.entity-publish-registry` — which duly turned up
# untracked in `git status` after a suite run.
/.entity-publish*
# Cargo.lock is COMMITTED (both of them). This repo ships binaries, not a
# library, and a release build must be reproducible: without the lockfile the
# same tag resolves different transitive versions on different days. Un-ignored
# 2026-08-17 as part of the release runway (RELEASE-READINESS §8).
src-tauri/target/

# Per-machine podman resource-cap overrides (RESOURCE-CAPS.md §4a) — never committed.
caps.local.mk
.tauri-home/
.cache/

# Python bytecode from tooling scripts
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Release artifacts (make dist / dist-web) — built, never committed.
/artifacts

# Local dev TLS (make serve TLS=1). Contains an unencrypted CA private key that
# test devices are told to trust — machine-local, never committed, never shared.
/.dev-certs/
